  <ym-title|Independent bounded review: cross-order Maxwell pairing
  separation><label|independent-bounded-review-cross-order-maxwell-pairing-separation>

  Reviewer: parent agent, session hairer-codex-existence-20261111, 12
  November 2026. Author: limits_draft in its isolated clone. The independent
  Astra reviewer identified the omitted source argument and suggested its
  source steps; this separate review checks the repaired argument directly.
  The parent did not edit or author the classifier candidate. This is not
  whole-unit acceptance.

  Candidate TeX SHA-256: <verbatim|7a02f08973d12c0487f410a3152bb6326127edc36adfabba9fc7c5f06ab7ec5e>.
  Evidence SHA-256: <verbatim|103c21635c98835b6c3cd214f36b06562aaa228b6b14a787b3d75a439e7129bc>.
  Source revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.

  <section|Scope and result><label|scope-and-result>

  Bounded pass for the new general separation argument, its order-one
  application, nontriviality of each sheet, and the finite-dimensional
  dual-span conclusion. The rest of the classifier is covered by the separate
  review, not this verdict. The required radial single-charge theorem is the
  previously independently reviewed canonical radial-flux chapter, with
  unchanged normalization.

  Read full <verbatim|Lean/YM/Next/MAXWELL/Flavor.lean>,
  <verbatim|Born.lean>, and <verbatim|Hidden.lean>; read the
  meaning-determining Sheet/Flavor/color maps in Paint.lean, polynomial wave
  and normalized coefficient identities in Jets.lean, radial_flux in
  Affine.lean, K_sample/K_right_D in Kernel.lean, and kernel_pole in
  Pole.lean. All qualified declarations are in <verbatim|YM.Maxwell.Free>.

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item><verbatim|Sheet h> is the real Maxwell solution-jet space;
    <verbatim|Flavor h> is its real dual. This is not an identification of
    invariant labels with all colored polynomials. <verbatim|fill> embeds a
    chosen scalar sheet in one fixed color.

    <item><verbatim|payment> tests the color-resolved pulse against all
    zero-order coordinate probes. Vanishing of those pairings makes every
    component of the pulse zero off its marked point. The compact cutoff
    derivative is supported away from that point, so the current flux
    vanishes. For any sheet A of order h,
    <verbatim|wavePoly>/<verbatim|asWave_jet> give a global homogeneous
    Maxwell wave whose normalized h-th Taylor coefficient is A.
    <verbatim|radial_flux> then gives zero = -(h+2)p(A). Since h+2 is nonzero
    and A is arbitrary, p=0. No positivity of an across-order pairing, and no
    distributional product at the pole, is assumed.

    <item>For the inductive step in <verbatim|ranging>, start with a
    lower-order probe q of order ell-1. Its derivative pairing is the
    higher-order test, with the sign from x-y absorbed in the derivative
    direction. The hypothesis kills these derivatives. <verbatim|kernel_pole>
    and Euler's identity yield -(4+h+ell-1)K(x)=0. The coefficient is
    nonzero; lower-order vanishing follows, and induction applies. The
    candidate now has the correct direction of this implication. It does not
    differentiate an already zero higher-order pairing to obtain a lower one.

    <item><verbatim|Born.has_sheet> argues by contradiction from
    <verbatim|Flavor.cell_alive>: if an order-c sheet were zero, all its
    probes would vanish, forcing the nonzero zero-order coordinate functional
    to vanish by the just-proved separation. This justifies choosing a probe
    and sheet with evaluation one at each of the distinct orders used in the
    determinant specialization.

    <item><verbatim|Hidden.probe_radius_span> uses all nonzero displacements
    and a fixed partner order. The zero-annihilator argument, the color
    decomposition and ordinary finite-dimensional duality justify the
    asserted span. It is not a span at one momentum or one displacement.
    Applying the resulting linear map to a basis yields all the polynomial
    partial derivatives, as in <verbatim|group_meal>.

    <item>In the panel argument the special case h=1, ell=0 is now tested
    against arbitrary A in S_1. Its radial factor is -3, so it annihilates
    the whole order-one functional. The erroneous earlier claim about
    zero-order waves testing the order-one sheet is absent from this
    candidate.
  </itemize-minus>

  <section|Actual checks and limits><label|actual-checks-and-limits>

  Scoped <verbatim|rg>, <verbatim|cat>, and <verbatim|sed> source reads and
  candidate excerpts; SHA-256 computed with <verbatim|shasum -a 256>. No Lean
  edit/build or axiom replay. The parent will run the integrated structural
  and LaTeX checks separately. The source argument has not been replaced by a
  new proof. This bounded review says nothing about the global
  selected-history binding, external trace estimates or complete
  existence-proof closure. Machine-readable unit approvals remain unset.

